.el .ds Aq '
.TH swarm-mr-review 1  "swarm 0.1.0" "Swarmgit manual"
.SH NAME
swarm\-mr\-review \- Approve a merge request or ask for changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBswarm mr review\fR [\fB\-\-approve\fR] [\fB\-R\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-\-request\-changes\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-message\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIMR\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Approve a merge request or ask for changes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-approve\fR
Approve the commits as they are now
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
A repo ID or link; by default the swarm remote of this clone
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Use what is already here instead of syncing first
.TP
\fB\-\-request\-changes\fR
Ask for changes; say which with \-m
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
What you think
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIMR\fR]
Its branch or ID (default: the current branch)
